<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐΐᾰχος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span> (i.e.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-ϝίαχος</span>) either, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			(from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> copul., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰαχή</span>) <i>joining in a shout,</i> or,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀν-</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> priv.) <i>noiseless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄβρομοι αὐΐαχοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.41
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				13.70
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνίαχοι</span> is
				v.l. in Il.l.c. and read by codd. in Q.S.l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
